# The Streamlit dashboard's own dependency set (v3 slice 3, owner decision S17; recompiled for Linux in v3 slice 4, T2, in
# notes/eg-new-feature/v3-slice4-cloud-run-deploy-2026-11-03.md): installed by `make setup`, CI's lint-and-test and the dashboard
# image (Dockerfile), never by the production workflows (score.yml, monitor.yml), which install requirements.txt. The constraint
# keeps every shared pin (pandas, numpy, pyarrow, google-cloud-bigquery, ...) equal to requirements.txt's; recompile with
# `make lock-dashboard` after every `make lock-main`. It compiles inside the Dockerfile's base image (linux/amd64), so the
# lockfile is the image's, and marks watchdog (required by streamlit off macOS; no macOS wheel for Python 3.14) Linux-only (F10).
# Each pin is a release at least 7 days old when added (the Dependabot cooldown rule): streamlit 1.66.1 (2026-10-21), altair
# 6.3.0 (2026-09-15); google-cloud-bigquery is requirements.txt's pin.
-c requirements.txt
streamlit==1.66.1
altair==6.3.0
google-cloud-bigquery==3.46.1
